{
  "note": "Lost Samples (docs/design/samples-definition.md). WMA Professional and Lossless streams gain Coded Samples (a frame length for each frame declared and in the file). Standard WMA streams off Microsoft's rule and Voice streams count their invalid frames and superframes at their declared samples and lose them: writer-stamp-last, writer-stamp-not-last and the first stream of fragments-in-two-streams (0 to 4,096; the second stream of fragments-in-two-streams has only lost frames and gains its Statistics node) and seven Voice fixtures, with the duration, the Voice statistics that read the totals and the stream's key lostSamples. A standard stream that had no duration gains Average Bitrate. The ASF container hands every incomplete media object to the codec parser flagged cut: voice-truncated.asf reads the superframe its cut last object finishes (24 superframes instead of 23, 11,060 samples instead of 10,760, nothing lost; wma.voice-unfinished is gone, wma.packet-short is new, and the bitrate falls with the longer duration). The cut standard files external-windows-wma92-cbr-stereo-44k-128-cut-30 and -cut-36 count the frames their first byte declares. The four derived cut and damaged fixtures are new and not listed.",
